# Float#abs

abs() -> Float

Get absolute value

```ruby
d = (a - b).abs
```

# Float#+

+(Integer | Float other) -> Float

Perform addition

```ruby
x + 1.0
```

# Float#===

===(untyped other) -> bool

Equality as `case` uses it

```ruby
case x
when 1.0 then hit
end
```

# Float#<=>

<=>(Integer | Float other) -> (Integer | nil)

Compare. Returns -1, 0 or 1

```ruby
a <=> b
```

# Float#/

/(Integer | Float other) -> Float

Perform division

Dividing by 0.0 does not raise; it gives Infinity.
```ruby
x / 2.0
```

# Float#==

==(untyped other) -> bool

Perform equality comparison

**Do not compare floats with ==**; rounding drifts. Compare the size of
the difference.
```ruby
(a - b).abs < 0.001
```

# Float#>=

>=(Integer | Float other) -> bool

Perform greater than or equal comparison

```ruby
if x >= 0.0
```

# Float#>

>(Integer | Float other) -> bool

Perform greater than comparison

```ruby
if x > 0.0
```

# Float#<=

<=(Integer | Float other) -> bool

Perform less than or equal comparison

```ruby
if x <= 1.0
```

# Float#<

<(Integer | Float other) -> bool

Perform less than comparison

```ruby
if x < 1.0
```

# Float#%

%(Integer | Float other) -> Float

Calculate modulo

```ruby
5.5 % 2.0  #=> 1.5
```

# Float#*

*(Integer | Float other) -> Float

Perform multiplication

```ruby
x * 0.5
```

# Float#**

**(Integer | Float other) -> Float

Calculate power

```ruby
2.0 ** 0.5
```

# Float#-

-(Integer | Float other) -> Float

Perform subtraction

```ruby
x - 1.0
```

# Float#-@

-@() -> Float

Unary minus operator. Inverts sign

```ruby
-x
```

# Float#+@

+@() -> Float

Unary plus operator. Returns self

```ruby
+x
```

# Float#to_f

to_f() -> Float

Return self as floating point number

Returns the number itself.
```ruby
x.to_f
```

# Float#to_i

to_i() -> Integer

Convert to integer (truncate)

**Truncates** rather than rounding; a negative number moves toward zero.
```ruby
1.9.to_i   #=> 1
(-1.9).to_i #=> -1
```

# Float#to_s

to_s() -> String

Convert to string

```ruby
x.to_s
```
